     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> 
     <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>Furthermore
    </section-heading>
    <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
       rolemaps-to="Part"
      >
     <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
        xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
        Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
        rolemaps-to="P"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>The reader could have forgotten all the nice acronyms, so we repeat the meaning again.
     </text-block>
    </semantic-para>
    <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
       rolemaps-to="Part"
      >
     <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
        xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
        Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
        rolemaps-to="P"
       >
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>If you want to know more about Global System for Mobile communication (
      <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
        >
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>GSM
       <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
      </Link>
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>), Time Division Multiple Access (
      <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
        >
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>TDMA
       <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
      </Link>
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>), Code Division Multiple Access (
      <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
        >
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>CDMA
       <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
      </Link>
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>) and other acronyms, just read a book about mobile communication. Just to mention it: There is another Used Acronym (
      <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
        >
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>UA
       <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
      </Link>
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>), just for testing purposes!
     </text-block>
    </semantic-para>
