      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>Some chemistry and physics
     </subsection-heading>
     <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
        rolemaps-to="Part"
       >
      <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
         xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
         Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
         rolemaps-to="P"
        >
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>Nicotinamide Adenine Dinucleotide (
       <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
         >
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>NAD
        <text-fragment xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
           xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
           Layout:TextPosition="Sup"
           rolemaps-to="Span"
          >
         <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>+
        </text-fragment>
        <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
       </Link>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>) is a major electron acceptor in the oxidation of fuel molecules. The reactive part of 
       <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
         >
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>NAD
        <text-fragment xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
           xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
           Layout:TextPosition="Sup"
           rolemaps-to="Span"
          >
         <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>+
        </text-fragment>
        <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
       </Link>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> is its nictinamide ring, a pyridine derivate.
      </text-block>
     </semantic-para>
     <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
        rolemaps-to="Part"
       >
      <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
         xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
         Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
         rolemaps-to="P"
        >
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>One mol consists of 
       <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
         >
        <Formula xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
           title="math"
           af="mathml-1.xml source.tex"
           xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
           Layout:Placement="Inline"
          >
          <AssociatedFile name="mathml-1.xml" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/mathml+xml" xmlns="">
          <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <msub> <mi>𝑁</mi> <mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi> </msub> </math>
          </AssociatedFile>
          <AssociatedFile name="source.tex" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/x-tex" xmlns="">
          $\relax N_{\mathrm A}$
          </AssociatedFile>
         <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>𝑁A
        </Formula>
        <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
       </Link>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> atoms or molecules. There is a relation between the constant of Boltzmann and the Number of Avogadro:
      </text-block>
      <Formula xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
         title="equation"
         af="mathml-2.xml source.tex"
         xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
         Layout:Placement="Block"
        >
        <AssociatedFile name="mathml-2.xml" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/mathml+xml" xmlns="">
        <math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mtable displaystyle="true" intent=":system-of-equations"> <mtr> <mtd intent=":equation-label"> <mtext> (1) </mtext> </mtd> <mtd intent=":pause-medium"> <mpadded depth="0" height="0"> <mtext/> </mpadded> <mrow/> <mi>𝑘</mi> <mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">=</mo> <mi>𝑅</mi> <mo lspace="0" rspace="0">/</mo> <mpadded depth="0" height="0"> <mtext/> </mpadded> <mtext> <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <msub> <mi>𝑁</mi> <mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi> </msub> </math> </mtext> </mtd> </mtr> </mtable> </math>
        </AssociatedFile>
        <AssociatedFile name="source.tex" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/x-tex" xmlns="">
        \begin {equation}k = R/\acs {NA}\label {my:eq}\end {equation}
        </AssociatedFile>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>𝑘=𝑅/
       <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
         >
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>𝑁A
        <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
       </Link>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>(1)
      </Formula>
     </semantic-para>
     <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
        rolemaps-to="Part"
       >
      <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
         xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
         Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
         rolemaps-to="P"
        >
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>Liquid Oxygen/Liquid Hydrogen (
       <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
         >
        <Formula xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
           title="math"
           af="mathml-3.xml source.tex"
