      </heading-number>
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> 
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>Some testing Integrated Circuits (
      <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
        >
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>IC
       <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
      </Link>
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>s) fundamentals
     </subsection-heading>
     <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
        rolemaps-to="Part"
       >
      <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
         xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
         Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
         rolemaps-to="P"
        >
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>When testing 
       <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
         >
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>IC
        <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
       </Link>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>s, one typically wants to identify functional blocks to be tested separately. The latter are commonly indicated as Blocks Under Test (
       <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
         >
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>BUT
        <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
       </Link>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>s). To test a 
       <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
         >
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>BUT
        <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
       </Link>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> requires defining a testing strategy… An 
       <Link xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
         >
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>IC
        <?ReferencedObject type="Annot" page="1" ?>
       </Link>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> popped up unexpectedly.
      </text-block>
     </semantic-para>
